encyclopedia :displaced_door_brace do
  name "Displaced-Door Brace"
  aka "brace", "door frame"
  kind :technology
  subkind :infrastructure
  status :complete
  topics :"fluid-reality", :danger, :rebuilding, :transport
  prevalence :uncommon
  appears_when all: { place: [:displacement_zone] }
  summary "A displaced-door brace is the displacement country's essential furniture: a sprung ringglass frame wedged into a doorway that has opened somewhere wrong, holding the two mismatched edges apart and honest while people and furniture move through. Cordon services stage them like fire equipment."
  function "Holds the mismatched edges of a displaced doorway stable and passable during crossings"
  classes "The standard household brace, the freight pattern with roller sills, and the cordon services' rapid frame that assembles under a rescue count"
  capacity "A set brace certifies one doorway for walking traffic; the freight pattern takes a handcart, and everything larger waits for the surveyors"
  operating_limit "A brace holds a settled mismatch and reports an unsettling one — the frame's tone climbs as the edges work — and brace discipline clears the door at the second tone"

  descriptive_identity(
    appearance: "A doorframe-sized rectangle of sprung ringglass members with broad shoe " \
                "plates, painted cordon orange, its corners carrying the tuning studs that " \
                "give a set brace its standing tone. Folded, it carries like a stretcher; " \
                "set, it looks like a doorway wearing a splint.",
    working: "The crew wedges the shoes against both edges of the mismatch, springs the " \
             "members to tension, and reads the frame's tone: a set brace hums low and " \
             "steady, and the hum is the certification that the doorway will hold its " \
             "present geometry while crossed.",
    risks: "The brace holds edges apart and holds them honest, and the second duty is the " \
           "load-bearing one — a mismatch beginning to move climbs the brace's tone, and " \
           "the discipline of leaving at the second tone is written in the incident " \
           "ledgers of everyone who taught it."
  )

  prose <<~PROSE
    In the displacement country — Xyloathax's shifted quarters, the galleries around Gray Line, anywhere the #{encyclopedia_ref :displaced_room_law, "displaced-room law"} runs — a doorway is an opinion the building may revise. When a door opens onto a room that arrived from elsewhere, the two edges of the opening rarely agree: floor heights offset by a hand, walls meeting at a lie of an angle, the seam between geometries working like pack ice. The displaced-door brace is the tool that makes such a doorway crossable. A sprung ringglass frame goes into the opening, shoe plates wedged to both edges, members tensioned until the brace takes the mismatch's argument into its own body — and the doorway, splinted, holds one shape long enough to be used.

    The brace's second function outranks its first. A set brace hums — the standing tone its tuning studs give the tensioned members — and the tone is a live report on the seam it straddles: steady means the mismatch is settled, a climbing tone means the geometries are working, and the second distinct tone-step is the order to clear the door, obeyed in brace country with the reflex Mareth gives its horn. Households in displacement quarters own a brace the way other households own a fire blanket, cordon services stage the rapid pattern at their posts and drill assembly under a spoken count, and the freight version with its roller sills moves the furniture of entire relocated rooms through openings that would otherwise ration a family's goods to what fits a crawl.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :operations, heading: "Setting, Certifying, and the Second Tone"
    Setting a brace is drilled craft: shoes to the true edges, spring to the count, tone check against the crew's fork. A set brace certifies the doorway for walking traffic — the cordon services chalk the certification on the lintel with the set time — and brace custom treats the hum as public information, the way sledge crews treat the mane: anyone passing a braced door is entitled to pause and listen, and the courteous crossing pauses anyway.

    The discipline's whole weight hangs on the second tone. A working seam climbs the brace's pitch in steps, the first step is a warning that reroutes freight and hurries stragglers, and the second clears the doorway outright — the brace stays, the people leave, and the incident ledgers of every cordon service explain in identical entries what happened the years anyone argued with it. Braces recovered from doors that finished their move are retired with respect and read like flight recorders: the deformation in the sprung members maps the seam's last argument, and the surveyors buy every one the services will sell.
  PROSE

  cue "The doorway wears an orange sprung frame like a splint, humming one low steady note, and traffic crosses through it at an ordinary pace with half an ear on the hum."
  cue "The brace's tone climbs one clear step, and the corridor reorganizes itself away from the door with drilled calm before the sentence being spoken is finished."
  affordance "A set brace turns a mismatched doorway into certified passage — chalked, humming, and honest — and the tone gives everyone in earshot a live reading on a seam that instruments would otherwise need a survey crew to watch."
  pressure "The brace certifies the present geometry and only the present geometry, so brace country lives inside its tone discipline — and the freight that must cross a first-tone door tests exactly the judgment the second tone exists to overrule."
  variation "Households keep the standard brace folded by the door like a fire blanket; cordon services drill the rapid pattern to a spoken count and time each other at festivals."
  variation "Retired braces from completed moves are read like flight recorders — the members' deformation maps the seam's last argument — and the survey offices buy every one the cordon services release."
end
